A||N||9||varnster||How to pull an alternator from an auto 87gt||||10||
Z||000000||varnster||08-08-2001||08:41 PM||||After much help from you guys it is finally out!he he. It WILL NOT drop out the bottom,<BR>or out the top, but out the wheel well. After<BR>pulling the ball joint and completly taking<BR>out the alternator bracket. This is the only<BR>way on a 87 auto v6 gt. Hope this helps others<BR>planing on this simple 30 min task (ya right)||||reg||10
Z||000001||Capt Fiero||08-08-2001||08:52 PM||||I am sorry I came into this thread a little late, but there is a neat trick to alternators on V6 Automatic fiero's I can re and re that is take out and have back in the car in under 30min.  When you get the alternator unhooked, it is very easy to move it around, it just wont come all the way out of the engine bay, well, on the back of the alt, there are 4, 8mm screwes.  You remove those screws and then the alternator comes out in 2 pieces.  Doing it this way, you dont have to do anything to any mounts just remove the pinch bolt first then the pivot bolt and unpluge the wires.  Once apart the install is really rather simple, push the brushes into there slots use a paper clip stuff through the back to hold the brushes in place.  You drop the new alternator back in, in 2 peices and assemble it all.   It may be a bit complex sounding for someone that has never taken an alternator apart before but it really is very simple.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lar||08-08-2001||10:20 PM||||It's been awhile since my 87SE with the alternator cooling fan and tubes, but on my 88 chassis with 3.4L V-6 you just...take alternator off bracket and lay it out of the way, then pull bracket and pull the center and right rear plug wires.  Comes out the top with no trouble in ten minutes.  Goes back in with new alternator setting above the muffler, installing bracket then alternator, and pluggin in plug wires and tightening belt.  Yeah, no way it was coming out the bottom without more work than I wanted to do.||||reg||1
Z||000003||CanadianGT||08-08-2001||11:51 PM||||Are 87 and 86 GT different?  I didnt think they were.  I just removed the alternator on mine, and I have an auto transmisson, and it was really fast. I brought mine out through the wheel well to.  At first I thought I would have to remove the ball joint, but instead I moved it to the right of the strut, and it slid out easily there.  Just to the right of the A- arm.<BR>PeACE <BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000004||LAMBO||08-09-2001||10:50 AM||||Sorry to here you had difficulties. But to reiterate, I've changed several V6 alternators, and all of them come out the top. From memory, remove front dog bone bolt, swing up. Remove cooling tube. Remove alt bolts. Disconnect alt. wiring. Remove alt. bracket bolts so that it lays loose. Pull alt. out the top. You may have to finese it a little, but it comes out, no problem. Actually its more like a 45 min. to 1 hour job start to finish. Especially while enjoying a cool one.<P>Important thing is, you got it done. Good job.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-09-2001||06:00 PM||||too bad your not around me, I could have changed it while you had a can of soda. Yes out the bottom for me, mines 86 4 speed but shouldnt make any dif, since its on opposite side of engine compt. do you have stock exhaust, if not that may be the difference.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Capt Fiero||08-09-2001||06:35 PM||||for those of you that have never had the experience, an automatic trans makes alternator a huge change, as the output shaft from the transaxle is much larger.  Take a look into an auto engine bay when you get a chance.||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnF||08-09-2001||06:56 PM||||To remove any part:<P>1.  Remove attaching hardware.<BR>2.  Turn car upside down.<BR>3.  Shake vigorously.<P>(The military way)||||reg||12
Z||000008||varnster||08-09-2001||07:44 PM||||GUYS,im telling you on MY car the brake lines and the studs for mounting the cooling <BR>tube to the firewall are in the way when you bring it out the top, and the tranny and exhaust are in the way droping it out the bottom, there IS NO WAY ANYONE CAN TAKE IT OUT ANY OTHER WAY THEN OUT THE WHEEL WELL!<BR>but I will have a six pack waiting for someone who can SHOW me how easy this can be done otherwise. thanks for all help!||||reg||7
Z||000009||rogergarrison||08-09-2001||07:53 PM||||Ill take your word for it capt. I never did it on an automatic myself. But Im still looking for a good condition V6 auto in my area for sale. ||||reg||1
